{
  "id": "household-live-updates",
  "title": "household-live-updates",
  "overview": "Provide the shared household live-update connection and initial schedule snapshot, and describe how received snapshots reconcile the displayed week and Today without implying lossless recovery or complete state convergence.",
  "requirementCount": 41,
  "requirements": [
    {
      "name": "Attempt the stream from the mounted app shell",
      "text": "The browser app shell SHALL attempt a credentialed connection to `/api/stream` on mounting. A nonempty public API base SHALL be concatenated with `/api/stream`; an absent or empty base SHALL use the relative path. Navigation retaining that shell SHALL retain its connection effect rather than create a page-specific connection.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Apply shared access and stream-specific member checks",
      "text": "GET `/api/stream` SHALL use the household-identity API access gate. After authorization it SHALL require a GUID-valued `x-family-member-id` cookie, returning 400 with member-cookie guidance when absent or unparseable. A member header alone SHALL NOT replace this cookie; this stream check SHALL NOT establish member existence.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Return a fresh connection identity with a successful snapshot",
      "text": "Each accepted stream request SHALL register a fresh connection identity before retrieving its initial snapshot. When retrieval and output succeed, it SHALL emit a `connected` event carrying `type: connected`, `schedule` and that `connectionId` directly in the frame data. Registration alone SHALL NOT establish successful emission, receipt or state application.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Read week zero on every accepted connection",
      "text": "The initial snapshot SHALL read the server's current week at offset zero on each accepted request, including a later reconnection. Its schedule SHALL contain seven Monday-through-Sunday day entries, week status, lock state and available persisted grocery state/items. It SHALL NOT select the browser's displayed offset or replay missed domain notifications.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Frame and maintain the open response",
      "text": "An accepted stream SHALL set `Content-Type: text/event-stream`, `Cache-Control: no-cache`, `Connection: keep-alive` and `X-Accel-Buffering: no`. Named data frames SHALL use an event line, a JSON data line and a blank-line terminator. After successful initial output, the controller SHALL attempt flushed `: ping` comment frames at fifteen-second timer ticks until cancellation or failure.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Keep browser connection failures bounded to the mounted effect",
      "text": "A connection-construction exception SHALL be logged and end that mounting attempt. A later connection error SHALL be logged without an application-created replacement connection, retry timer or store reset. Reconnection attempts SHALL be delegated to the browser's native connection while it remains eligible; no successful reconnect deadline is established.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Dispatch received connected snapshots without resetting optimistic guards",
      "text": "On a successfully parsed `connected` event, the browser SHALL retain a supplied truthy connection identity, pass the schedule to displayed-week reconciliation and then attempt Today reconciliation. Receipt SHALL NOT clear optimistic guards or confirm pending move sequences merely because a connection opened. Without a supplied identity it SHALL retain any existing identity.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Reconcile only the displayed snapshot week",
      "text": "A snapshot without a move echo SHALL replace or merge displayed-week state only when its week offset matches the loaded week, treating an omitted offset as zero. A different offset SHALL leave that week's state unchanged. The independent Today reconciliation SHALL remain eligible even if displayed-week reconciliation ignores the snapshot.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Defer day replacement during local moves",
      "text": "A matching snapshot without a move echo SHALL defer day replacement while a drag is active or a local move is unconfirmed, retaining the latest deferred snapshot while applying incoming week status and advancing the synchronization timestamp. Reconnection alone SHALL NOT release this deferral.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Preserve existing day content under snapshot merge guards",
      "text": "An eligible snapshot SHALL preserve prior pending suggestion content for the same date when no persisted recipe or non-cooking entry replaces it. If every normalized incoming day lacks a recipe, it SHALL also retain prior recipes and their statuses for matching ordinary dates and retain existing week status when prior days exist. Persisted recipes and non-cooking entries SHALL take precedence for their dates.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Apply available snapshot adjuncts conditionally",
      "text": "An eligible nondeferred snapshot SHALL replace grocery items and any supplied raw or generated-client boolean check dictionary. Explicit false values and empty dictionaries SHALL be retained. Missing or null check-state SHALL retain loaded checks. Existing absolute-week, move-echo and optimistic deferral guards SHALL apply before replacement.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Select Today independently from the received snapshot",
      "text": "After displayed-week reconciliation returns, a connected snapshot SHALL offer Today an update only when its days include the deployment-local current date. It SHALL supply that entry's recipe or null, status or zero and non-cooking metadata or null. An absent current-date entry SHALL leave Today unchanged through this handler.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Preserve Today's recent optimistic recipe guard",
      "text": "Today SHALL suppress an offered update with a different recipe identity while its optimistic write is less than two seconds old. Otherwise it SHALL apply recipe and status, retain non-cooking metadata only for status three and clear the optimistic timestamp. Matching recipe identity SHALL permit detail updates inside the guard window. Suppressed updates SHALL NOT be queued for timed replay.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Use connection identity only for immediate echo exclusion",
      "text": "Subsequent requests through the shared API client SHALL attach a stored nonempty connection identity as `X-SSE-Connection-ID`. At publication boundaries that pass that header through as exclusion, broadcasts SHALL skip the matching current registration and attempt other registrations. A missing or obsolete identity SHALL NOT identify a different newly registered connection for exclusion.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Bound delivery to current process registrations",
      "text": "Publication SHALL attempt named frames only for responses registered in the current process, serializing each broadcast write through that registration's broadcast lock. A caught response write or flush failure SHALL remove that registration. This SHALL NOT establish serialization with controller snapshot/heartbeat writes, durable delivery, subscriber acknowledgement or cross-process propagation.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Forward received vote totals to existing consumers",
      "text": "A parsed `vote_updated` event SHALL offer its recipe identity and vote count first to the displayed-week consumer and then to Discovery, provided preceding steps return. Matching loaded planner recipes SHALL receive that recipe vote count without creating missing entries. Discovery SHALL receive the same update for its own interest and ranking policy; vote meaning remains owned by recipe discovery.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Filter received smart defaults by their nested week",
      "text": "A parsed `smart_defaults_updated` event SHALL offer its defaults for application only when `defaults.weekOffset` strictly equals the loaded week offset. A different or absent nested offset SHALL leave the displayed schedule unchanged through this handler. The outer event offset SHALL NOT override this gate.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Reconcile received suggestions without replacing occupied slots",
      "text": "Eligible smart defaults SHALL fill empty or pending displayed slots by day index, retaining supplied recipe display data and pending vote metadata. Persisted recipe slots and status-three non-cooking slots SHALL remain unchanged. A pending slot absent from the new defaults SHALL clear its suggestion and pending vote metadata. This consequence SHALL NOT assign a recipe on the server or define consensus eligibility.",
      "scenarios": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Attempt invalidation at supported schedule publication boundaries",
      "text": "The server SHALL attempt `fill_the_gap_invalidated` for the affected week after assignment or removal of an existing dated entry reaches its preceding week-publication boundary successfully. The unscheduled-cooking validation branch SHALL attempt this invalidation after saving cooking history. An available request connection exclusion SHALL be forwarded; invalidation SHALL NOT imply refreshed candidate data.",
      "scenarios": []
